; A balance assertion sums the subtree's lots in one inventory, as beancount
; does: lots of one key from different accounts merge and drop when they sum
; to zero, so 60.00 USD here and -60.00 USD there leave 0 and the difference
; from 1 USD is -1 USD, not -1.00 USD; lots of different keys keep their
; digits.
2020-01-01 open Assets:Bank
2020-01-01 open Assets:Stock
2020-01-01 open Assets:Mixed
2020-01-01 open Assets:Bank:Checking
2020-01-01 open Assets:Bank:Savings
2020-01-01 open Assets:Stock:Long
2020-01-01 open Assets:Stock:Short
2020-01-01 open Assets:Mixed:Long
2020-01-01 open Assets:Mixed:Short
2020-01-01 open Equity:O

2020-01-02 * "cash across two accounts"
  Assets:Bank:Checking   60.00 USD
  Assets:Bank:Savings    40.00 USD
  Assets:Bank:Checking  -100.00 USD

2020-01-03 balance Assets:Bank  1 USD

2020-01-02 * "one lot key across two accounts"
  Assets:Stock:Long    10.00 HOOL {1 USD}
  Assets:Stock:Short  -10.00 HOOL {1 USD}

2020-01-03 balance Assets:Stock  1 HOOL

2020-01-02 * "two lot keys across two accounts"
  Assets:Mixed:Long    10.00 HOOL {1 USD}
  Assets:Mixed:Short  -10.00 HOOL {2 USD}
  Equity:O

2020-01-03 balance Assets:Mixed  1 HOOL
